BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blackbird-foundation-believers-fund-iii-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Blackbird Foundation: Believers Fund III 2026
DESCRIPTION:Believers funds the people\, projects and programs creating the
  conditions for young people's creativity to flourish at scale. Creativity
  is meant in the broadest sense: artists are creative\, but so are scienti
 sts\, debaters\, community builders and dancers\, and a project can be any
 thing from a summer camp to a robotics competition to a co-working holiday
  house for artists.\n\nOrganisation: Blackbird Foundation\nLocation: Austr
 alia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisations establishe
 d in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 and A
 UD 10\,000 grants. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects must be complet
 ed within 12 months\n\nMore: https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisatio
 ns established in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-future-leaders-bitsummit-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART:20261105T053000Z
DTEND:20261105T060000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 AEDT: Screen Australia Future Leaders Delegation: Bi
 tSummit 2027 (Kyoto)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 05 Nov 2026 at 17:00 AEDT.\n\nScreen Australia's Future 
 Leaders Delegation sends up to eight early-to-mid career Australian gamema
 kers to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, one of Asia's l
 eading independent games festivals.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLoc
 ation: Delegation to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, wi
 th a pre-departure workshop in Melbourne. Open to Australian citizens or p
 ermanent residents\, or incorporated Australian companies.\nAward: AUD 6\,
 000 per delegate towards flights\, accommodation\, event tickets\, ground 
 transportation and meals\, plus covered travel costs for the pre-departure
  workshop and the opportunity to exhibit a game on the Australia stand. Up
  to eight delegates.\nDuration: BitSummit runs 21-23 May 2027 in Kyoto\; m
 andatory pre-departure workshop in Melbourne in mid-April 2027\n\nMore: ht
 tps://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/future-leaders-delegation-bitsummit-
 2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/future-leaders-delegation-bitsu
 mmit-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Delegation to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, w
 ith a pre-departure workshop in Melbourne. Open to Australian citizens or 
 permanent residents\, or incorporated Australian companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-global-fellowships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART:20270211T053000Z
DTEND:20270211T060000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 AEDT: Screen Australia Global Fellowships (AUD 80\,0
 00-100\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 11 Feb 2027 at 17:00 AEDT.\n\nScreen Australia's Global 
 Fellowships support Australian screen practitioners (producers\, directors
 \, writers and development executives) pursuing international professional
  development and career acceleration through placements with leading globa
 l screen organizations.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLocation: Inter
 national placements with leading global screen organizations\, self-arrang
 ed by the fellow. Open to Australian citizens or permanent residents (sole
  traders) or incorporated Australian companies.\nAward: Non-recoupable gra
 nts of AUD 80\,000 (single continuous placement of up to 6 months) or AUD 
 100\,000 (multiple placements over up to 12 months)\, plus up to AUD 5\,00
 0 for carers' and/or accessibility costs. Up to 10 fellows annually.\nDura
 tion: Placements of up to 6 months (single) or up to 12 months (multiple)\
 n\nMore: https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/global-fellowships/?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/global-fellowships/?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International placements with leading global screen organizations\
 , self-arranged by the fellow. Open to Australian citizens or permanent re
 sidents (sole traders) or incorporated Australian companies.
END:VEVENT
